## Safe applicability-candidate handoff and execution

Phase 104 adds a bounded, explicit consumption path for an already selected applicability candidate.

The path is:

```text
applicability candidate
↓
candidate selection / source-scoped reduction
↓
RepositoryGeneratorApplicabilityCandidateHandoff
↓
execution-catalog validation
↓
READY validation
↓
explicit validated final rule
↓
bounded producer search
↓
RepositoryGeneratorApplicabilityHandoffSearchReport
↓
same prebuilt BoundedProducerSearchReport object
↓
same selected producer path
↓
same selected final rule
↓
execution
↓
actual producer ProofStep objects
↓
actual goal ProofStep
```

Phase 104 deliberately keeps these distinctions:

```text
candidate filtering != theorem ranking
candidate selection != proof success
candidate handoff != automatic proof execution
applicability compatibility != theorem truth
```

The execution adapter does not rerun final-rule selection, producer selection, retry, or bounded search. Search-time `max_depth`, retry policy, and execution-catalog checks are consumed before execution.

The central identity invariants are:

```text
candidate rule
is validation.execution_entry.rule
is search_result.final_rule
is goal_step.inference_rule
```

and

```text
execution_result.report
is search_report.report
```

For selected producers:

```text
producer_node.producer_rule
is executed_producer_step.inference_rule
```

`GOAL_ALREADY_AVAILABLE` preserves the candidate / validation provenance but executes no producer or final rule.

Repository snapshot/versioning and stale-search-report detection are not part of Phase 104.

